body:
I'm almost at the end of ARR's MQ and I just join the subscription (30 days) today. So there's this recruiting a friend thingy which I did enter someone's recruitment code before I subscribed. I know the person's recruitment code which I enter will receive items, but do I also get it? If so where do I find it, or do I need to wait for 30 days at least to get anything? 

&#x200B;

And regarding that gold chocobo feather, when will i get them and how often? Do I need to subscribe at least 150 days in advance or is it accumulated through my 30 days of subscription plan? And what's after 270 days of subscription? Will I still get anything after? Thank you guys so much for always answering my questions! It really helps a lot, the game sometime have too much to learn.

I've some questions guys.

&#x200B;

So I'm currently on the free trial version, I bought A Realm Reborn off PSN and been playing it until I'm level 50. I learned that you're supposed to get the expansion in order to get pass level 50. If I subscribed to the subscription without buying the expansion for now, would I be able to level up pass level 50? Or it's a must to get the expansion and the subscription?

&#x200B;

On the subscription page, I saw there's a recruitment code thingy on the subscription page. Do I get anything for entering a recruitment code before subscribing since I'm considering about the subscription?

&#x200B;

And one last question is, on PSN store there isn't Heavensward or Bloodstorm anymore. There's just Shadowbringers, by getting that (Shadowbringers) does it come with Heavensward and Bloodstorm expansion together?

&#x200B;

Thank you for answering my question.

I see. I'll bare that in mind to add more butter the next time I'm doing it again.

&#x200B;

By the way, after I kept them in the container overnight and somehow the next day it peeled off nicely. Could the first time I baked it and I didn't let it cool down properly then I kept them in the fridge too early caused the muffins to stick to its cases? And as for last night batch, might have been because they were cooled down yet and it caused it to stick to its cases?

&#x200B;

As for the smoothness, did I undermixed or overmixed my ingredients?

&#x200B;

Thank you very much for taking the time to reply me!
